1
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:09,040
An introduction to communication
management.

2
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:15,800
So information needs of our stakeholders
needs to be relevant, timely, via the

3
00:00:15,801 --> 00:00:19,140
correct medium and addressing the proper
audience.

4
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:24,500
So only relevant information should be
communicated to appropriate stakeholders.

5
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:30,400
Not all information is communicated to all
stakeholders.

6
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:37,440
And please note that we spend at least 90%
of our time, communicating, which is why

7
00:00:37,441 --> 00:00:41,200
we live in meetings or we're back typing
up reports.

8
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:42,613
All right.

9
00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:44,880
So I want to point out a couple things.

10
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:47,000
We have effective communication.

11
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:50,940
That's giving the right
information to the right

12
00:00:50,941 --> 00:00:54,080
stakeholders at the right
time via the correct medium.

13
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:59,440
Whereas efficient communication means
giving only the information needed.

14
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:01,600
No more, no less.

